From 90b3a5c579ffb0ac164e4cea7163228a864ef0c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ross Cawston <rcawston@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Feb 2026 14:35:17 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/20] media: synopsys: hdmirx: fix buffer overflow on repeated HDMI-RX replug

Imported from https://github.com/rcawston/rockchip-rk3588-mainline-patches
at e13a311d8ee5e8ed92ec3d4a57c21f766c61d660, file 0003-rockchip-rk3588-hdmirx-plugout-fix-v1.patch.

Authored by Ross Cawston. This CeraLive copy re-packages the file as a git
mailbox so it can be applied with `git am`. Every added and removed line is
byte-identical to upstream's; scripts/verify-payload-parity.py enforces that.

Dropped 1 payload-free "Binary files .../.DS_Store ... differ"
stanza(s) that macOS left in the original `diff -ruN` output. They carry
no data, and git apply refuses a binary stanza with no index line.

NOT upstream-bound: this is a CeraLive-maintained adaptation, not a submission
to rockchip-rk3588-mainline-patches. No Signed-off-by is added, because none
was given upstream and inventing one would misattribute a DCO assertion.

---
diff -ruN aa/drivers/media/platform/synopsys/hdmirx/snps_hdmirx.c bb/drivers/media/platform/synopsys/hdmirx/snps_hdmirx.c
--- aa/drivers/media/platform/synopsys/hdmirx/snps_hdmirx.c	2026-02-09 14:27:48
+++ bb/drivers/media/platform/synopsys/hdmirx/snps_hdmirx.c	2026-02-09 14:27:56
@@ -619,6 +619,8 @@
 
 static void hdmirx_plugout(struct snps_hdmirx_dev *hdmirx_dev)
 {
+	struct hdmirx_stream *stream = &hdmirx_dev->stream;
+
 	if (!hdmirx_dev->plugged)
 		return;
 
@@ -639,6 +641,17 @@
 			   PHY_PDDQ, HDMI_DISABLE);
 	hdmirx_writel(hdmirx_dev, PHYCREG_CONFIG0, 0x0);
 	cancel_delayed_work(&hdmirx_dev->delayed_work_res_change);
+
+	/*
+	 * If V4L2 streaming was active when we killed DMA, signal a
+	 * fatal error on the vb2 queue so that any blocked DQBUF
+	 * returns immediately with POLLERR/POLLHUP instead of
+	 * hanging on EAGAIN until userspace timeout.
+	 */
+	mutex_lock(&hdmirx_dev->stream_lock);
+	if (vb2_is_streaming(&stream->buf_queue))
+		vb2_queue_error(&stream->buf_queue);
+	mutex_unlock(&hdmirx_dev->stream_lock);
 
 	/* will be NULL on driver removal */
 	if (hdmirx_dev->rgb_range)
